---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import PartIllustration from '../../components/PartIllustration.astro';
import { machinedParts } from '../../data/machined-parts';
---
<BaseLayout title="Custom CNC Machined Parts for OEM Production" description="Explore drawing-based brackets, blocks, shafts, bushings, connectors and housings for OEM applications. Send your requirements for a CNC machining review.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero parts-hero">
      <div class="container parts-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">MACHINED PARTS / OEM COMPONENTS</span>
          <h1>Your drawing.<br/>Your application.<br/><em>Your part.</em></h1>
          <p>Custom CNC-milled and turned components for industrial equipment. Explore part families, then share your drawing, quantity and requirements for review.</p>
          <a class="button button-orange" href="#part-families">Explore part families <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-drawing"><span>PART STUDY / 01</span><PartIllustration kind="mounting-brackets" /><p>Mounting bracket · Illustrative geometry</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="part-families" aria-labelledby="parts-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="parts-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">BUILT TO YOUR REQUIREMENTS</span><h2 id="parts-heading">A starting point for<br/><em>your next component.</em></h2></div><p>These part families help you describe your machining needs. Illustrations are conceptual examples, not photographs or completed customer projects. Each enquiry is assessed against actual capability.</p></div>
        <nav class="part-jumps" aria-label="Part families">{machinedParts.map(part => <a href={`#${part.id}`}>{part.title}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</nav>
        <div class="parts-grid">
          {machinedParts.map((part, index) => <article class="part-card" id={part.id}>
            <div class="part-visual"><span class="part-index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')} / PART FAMILY</span><PartIllustration kind={part.id}/>{part.process === 'CNC Milling' ? <a class="part-process" href="/services/cnc-milling/" aria-label={`CNC Milling services for ${part.title}`}>{part.process}</a> : <span class="part-process">{part.process}</span>}<span class="illustration-label">CONCEPT ILLUSTRATION</span></div>
            <div class="part-copy"><p class="part-application">{part.application}</p><h3>{part.title}</h3><p>{part.description}</p><h4>What we review with your drawing</h4><ul>{part.features.map(feature => <li>{feature}</li>)}</ul><a class="text-link" href={`/contact/?part=${part.id}#rfq-form`} aria-label={`Request similar components: ${part.title}`}>Request similar components <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          </article>)}
        </div>
        <p class="parts-note">Material grade, dimensions, tolerances, finishes and batch suitability are confirmed during drawing review. The examples above are not standard stocked products.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section section-soft"><div class="container"><SectionHeading eyebrow="FROM PART FAMILY TO PRODUCTION" title="The details that define your part" text="A part name is only the beginning. Share the specifications that matter to its function and assembly."/>
      <div class="requirements-grid"><article><span>01 / GEOMETRY</span><h3>Drawing & revision</h3><p>Provide a dimensioned drawing and, where available, a 3D model. Identify the revision and critical mating features.</p></article><article><span>02 / REQUIREMENTS</span><h3>Material & inspection</h3><p>Specify material grade, surface treatment, critical tolerances and any inspection records needed for the order.</p><a class="text-link" href="/quality/">Quality approach <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article><span>03 / PRODUCTION</span><h3>Quantity & delivery</h3><p>Tell us the initial batch quantity, target delivery and whether repeat orders are expected.</p><a class="text-link" href="/services/#production">Production approach <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container parts-faq"><SectionHeading eyebrow="BEFORE YOU ENQUIRE" title="A few practical answers"/>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details><summary>Can I order a part shown on this page?</summary><p>These are illustrative part families. Components are quoted to your drawings and agreed specifications rather than sold as catalogue items.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if my component is not shown here?</summary><p>Send your drawing through the RFQ form and select the relevant process, or choose “Not sure — please review”. The illustrations do not cover every possible geometry.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you review small batches and repeat orders?</summary><p>The intended focus is low-volume OEM production, with indicative batches around 20–500 pieces. Suitability and any repeat-order arrangements depend on the part and production review.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What tolerances and materials can you support?</summary><p>Include the material grade and tolerances on your drawing. Feasibility depends on geometry, size, process and inspection conditions; final requirements must be confirmed during quotation.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="cta-section"><div class="container cta-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">HAVE SOMETHING SIMILAR?</span><h2>Let’s start with<br/><em>your drawing.</em></h2><p>Share your component, material and quantity. We’ll review the requirements and clarify the next steps.</p></div><a class="button button-orange button-large" href="/contact/">Request a Quote <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .parts-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr 1fr;align-items:center;gap:60px}.parts-hero h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,66px)}.parts-hero .button{margin-top:12px}.hero-drawing{border:1px solid #40516a;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#223a57,#14263e);padding:24px;color:#506b88}.hero-drawing>span,.hero-drawing>p{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#bdccdb;margin:0}.hero-drawing :global(svg){display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.hero-drawing>p{letter-spacing:.5px}
  .parts-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:70px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:35px}.parts-intro h2{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,44px);line-height:1.2;margin:14px 0 0}.parts-intro h2 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--orange)}.parts-intro>p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}.part-jumps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-bottom:40px}.part-jumps a{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:10px 15px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;display:inline-flex;gap:15px;align-items:center}.part-jumps a:hover{border-color:var(--orange)}.part-jumps span{color:var(--orange)}
  .parts-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px}.part-card{border:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}.part-visual{position:relative;background-color:var(--soft);background-image:linear-gradient(#e3e8ee80 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,#e3e8ee80 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:28px 28px;padding:30px 24px 42px;color:#415d7b}.part-visual :global(svg){display:block;width:100%;height:230px}.part-index{position:absolute;top:18px;left:22px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:var(--muted)}.part-process{position:absolute;bottom:17px;left:22px;background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:3px 9px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700}.illustration-label{position:absolute;bottom:21px;right:22px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--muted)}
  .part-copy{padding:30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1}.part-application{font-size:12px!important;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a74b19!important;margin-bottom:10px}.part-copy h3{font-size:27px;letter-spacing:-.8px;margin:0 0 13px}.part-copy p{font-size:16px;color:var(--muted)}.part-copy h4{font-size:14px;margin:8px 0}.part-copy ul{padding-left:19px;margin:0 0 26px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}.part-copy li{padding:3px 0}.part-copy li::marker{color:var(--orange)}.part-copy .text-link{margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:14px}.parts-note{margin:28px 0 0;padding-left:18px;border-left:2px solid var(--orange);color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
  .requirements-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:30px}.requirements-grid article{border-top:2px solid var(--orange);padding-top:22px}.requirements-grid article>span{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:1px}.requirements-grid h3{font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.6px;margin:17px 0 12px}.requirements-grid p{color:var(--muted)}.parts-faq{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;gap:70px}.faq-list details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px 0}.faq-list details:first-child{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.faq-list summary{font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;padding-right:14px}.faq-list details p{color:var(--muted);margin:15px 0 0}.part-jumps a:focus-visible,.part-card a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--orange);outline-offset:4px}
  @media(max-width:900px){.parts-hero-grid{gap:30px}.parts-intro{gap:35px}.parts-faq{gap:30px}.part-copy{padding:24px}.requirements-grid{gap:22px}}
  @media(max-width:700px){.parts-hero-grid,.parts-intro,.parts-grid,.requirements-grid,.parts-faq{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.parts-hero-grid{gap:35px}.hero-drawing :global(svg){max-height:230px}.parts-intro{gap:20px}.parts-grid{gap:24px}.part-visual{padding-inline:15px}.part-visual :global(svg){height:215px}.part-copy{padding:24px}.part-copy h3{font-size:25px}.part-jumps{gap:8px}.part-jumps a{padding:8px 11px;font-size:12px;gap:8px}.illustration-label{right:14px;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.5px}.part-process{left:14px}.requirements-grid{gap:30px}.parts-faq{gap:0}}
</style>
